<title>UK: NatWest cuts Shell 5-yr div forecast 0.5p.</title>
<headline>NatWest cuts Shell 5-yr div forecast 0.5p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Securities has cut 0.5 pence from its dividend forecast for Royal Dutch Shell through to the year 2000, citing sterling/guilder rate changes as the cause, market sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The change is half a pence off all the dividend forecasts going to 2000, mainly as a result of new currency change forecasts,&quot; sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;The average currency rate was 2.55 sterling/guilder which has been revised to 2.65,&quot; the sources added.</p>
<p>The change means Natwest's dividend forecast for Shell drops to 37p for 1996 and 40 pence the year after.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
